From ace572683883afbb9edc9bb006739d32fc2a9942 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:59:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 237/241] hir_typeck: an inherent impl matched through a projection
 isn't deferred

tokio 1.21.2 (jlq 0.1.0) runtime/task/list.rs:142:

    let first_task = { let mut lock = self.inner.lock(); ..; lock.list.pop_back() };
    match first_task {
        Some(task) => task.shutdown(),
        None => return,
    }
    loop { .. }

    error:0: Type mismatch - ! != ()

`pop_back` lives in `impl<L: Link> LinkedList<L, L::Target>`. The
receiver `LinkedList<Task<S>, Header>` has no ivars, but the projection
in the impl type makes match_test_generics_fuzz answer Fuzzy, and
visit_call_populate_cache_UfcsInherent deferred the call as "only
matches by binding receiver ivars" until the fallback revisits. Those
run after the ivar fallbacks: the match ivar's only possibility was the
`return` arm's `!` (the call's result still unknown), the final fallback
picked it, and the call then resolved to `()`.

A receiver without ivars can only match fuzzily through a projection,
which find_method already expanded and compared (Equal); nothing is
pending, so the call commits at once, as rustc does. Receivers with
ivars keep the deferral.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hir_typeck/expr_cs__enum.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs__enum.cpp b/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs__enum.cpp
index 4a2c4f3a..01ce262f 100644
--- a/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs__enum.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs__enum.cpp
@@ -451,7 +451,12 @@ namespace typecheck
         }
         assert(impl_ptr);
         DEBUG("Found impl" << impl_ptr->m_params.fmt_args() << " " << impl_ptr->m_type);
-        if( defer_fuzzy_inherent )
+        // A receiver without ivars can only match fuzzily through a projection in the impl type (`impl<L: Link>
+        // LinkedList<L, L::Target>`), which find_method already expanded and matched: nothing is pending, so commit.
+        // Deferred to the fallback revisits, the call's result ivar reached the ivar fallbacks first: tokio 1.21.2
+        // runtime/task/list.rs:142 `match lock.list.pop_back() { Some(task) => task.shutdown(), None => return }` as
+        // a statement got `!` from the `return` arm, then "Type mismatch - ! != ()" against `shutdown`'s `()`.
+        if( defer_fuzzy_inherent && context.m_ivars.type_contains_ivars(e.type) )
         {
             // Does this impl only apply if ivars in the receiver resolve a particular way? (`impl Foo<Bar>` seen
             // through `Foo<_>`, or `impl<T> E<T,T>` through `E<_,_>`). Committing now would bind those ivars, while
